  data:  # 7399
    kind: work_item  # 7399
    title: "scip-python backend indexes an empty scratch dir: invoke passes the project positionally, which scip-python 0.6.6 ignores (it indexes --cwd)"  # 7399
    status: todo_hard  # 7399
    priority: 1  # 7399
    parent:  # 7399
    tags:  # 7399
    - scip  # 7399
    - multi_fidelity  # 7399
    - analysis_quality  # 7399
    - receiver_typing  # 7399
    isbefore: []  # 7399
    duplicate_of: []  # 7399
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 7399
    pr_ref:  # 7399
    description: "FOUND 2026-10-19 while implementing WI-losig (measuring a scip-python self-map). The scip-python backend has never indexed the analysed repository through hypergumbo.\n\nFACTS (scip-python 0.6.6, the pinned version):\n- invoke.run_scip_python_index runs `scip-python index <project> --project-name N --output <scratch>/index.scip` with the subprocess cwd set to a fresh scratch directory.\n- scip-python 0.6.6 takes NO positional project argument (`scip-python index --help`: options only; the project is `--cwd <path>`, default the process cwd). It silently ignores the positional and indexes its cwd: the run log says \"Indexing <scratch dir>\", \"Total Project Files 0\", exits 0 and writes a 72-75 byte index.\n- So every opted-in run indexes the empty scratch directory. On dev (whole hypergumbo repo, HYPERGUMBO_SCIP_PYTHON=1, binary on PATH): the scip_python pass ran 2.3 s, emitted 0 nodes, and the map was node-for-node identical to the plain map (61,431 nodes / 244,545 edges both).\n- The analyzer saw it -- it warns \"produced no symbols ... despite .py files being present\" -- but recorded silence_reason no_candidate_construct, which is ROUTINE (counted, not named, in the [passes] summary line), so the pass looked like it ran clean.\n- Why the tests missed it: test_scip_python_invoke.py pins the argv (it pinned the broken one) through an injected runner; the recorded fixtures were produced outside invoke.py.\n\nFIX: pass `--cwd <project>` (output stays an absolute path in the scratch dir, so the project is not written to); an empty index on a repo with .py files is `unreported` (CANNOT-DETERMINE), not a routine silence.\n\nSECOND GAP, same measurement: with --cwd fixed, indexing the whole repo (1,722 .py files) aborts in node with \"FatalProcessOutOfMemory\" after 170 s at 4.2 GB RSS (default V8 heap). Being measured with a larger heap; record the result here."  # 7399
    fields: {}  # 7399
